      "id": 1,
      "text": "South Williamsport celebrated the centennial of its incorporation as a borough in 1986.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Williamsport%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough was officially incorporated on November 29, 1886, when the villages of Rocktown, Billman, and nearby areas joined together.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Williamsport%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first settler in what is now South Williamsport was Aaron Hagerman, a transplanted Hollander who arrived shortly after the Revolutionary War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Williamsport%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hagermans Run, the stream that flows through the borough, bears the name of that early pioneer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Williamsport%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "South Williamsport is famous for hosting the Little League World Series every year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Williamsport%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The South Williamsport Area Historical Collection, dedicated to preserving the borough’s heritage, was formed on June 28, 2018.",
